  "text": "The Hopua te Nihotetea Detention Dam is a flood management asset located in the Northland region of New Zealand. It is designed to temporarily store floodwaters to reduce peak flows downstream, thereby mitigating the risk of river flooding. The dam is integrated with the Northland Regional Council's Environmental Data Hub, which includes a public-facing webcam to enhance situational awareness and emergency management.",
